    ERR_CMD_UNKNOWN for an enabled row pointing at Xcp_CmdNotImplemented exactly as it does for a
    disabled one" -- plus a paragraph deferring its own correction, on the grounds that neither row
    was the task at hand's own change. Both are deleted rather than re-deferred, because the claim is
    now false of every PGM row without exception: SP4c completes SP4, and with it the whole PGM
    command group, so in a gate-ON build all ELEVEN PGM PIDs point at real handlers in Xcp_PIDTable
    (source/Xcp.c), whose Xcp_CmdNotImplemented entries for those PIDs now survive only in the
