{#- Final review F4. PROGRAM_START reports this as MAX_BS_PGM (source/Xcp_Pgm.c) -- the PER-
    CONFIGURATION value, matching maxBS/minST immediately above, both of which are
    already the live field this build is actually running rather than a build-wide bound. Unlike
    them, this one also has a compile-time twin, XCP_PGM_MAX_BLOCK_SIZE (script/header_cfg.h.jinja2),
    which sizes Xcp_Internal.pgm_block -- and MUST stay the build-wide largest across every
    configuration, since the sources compile once for all of them. The two serve different masters
    on purpose: the buffer has to hold the biggest block ANY configuration in this build can ask
    for, but the response must promise only what THIS configuration actually offers, or a build
    holding a max_block_size=1 configuration beside a max_block_size=200 one would have the first
    advertise a block size the second's buffer allows but the first's own master was never told
    to expect.

    Conditioned on programming.enabled -- unlike maxBS/minST immediately above, which
    are not PGM-specific and were never at risk of this -- for the identical reason the PROGRAM/
    PROGRAM_NEXT ctoInfo minimum nibbles are conditioned on it two Task reviews running (Task 3
    finding 4, Task 4's own fix round 1 finding 2, both now generalised into
    test_gate_off_output_does_not_depend_on_any_other_programming_setting,
    test/pgm_configuration_test.py): with the gate off, this row is unread either way
    (source/Xcp_Pgm.c's own reader is entirely inside #if XCP_FLASH_PROGRAMMING_ENABLED), but an
    UNCONDITIONAL fold on programming.max_block_size would still change Xcp_Cfg.c whenever that
    setting changes, real byte differences that property test exists specifically to catch --
    caught here, during this very fix, the first time this row was built without the conjunction:
    keyed on programming.max_block_size alone, programming_max_block_size=1
    (test_gate_off_output_does_not_depend_on_any_other_programming_setting's own variant) failed
    immediately. 0, not 8 (the schema's own default `| default(8)` gives when the whole
    programming block is absent), is the value emitted whenever the gate is off: this row is
    inert either way, and 0 needs no further fold with the field's own default -- unlike
    XCP_PGM_MAX_BLOCK_SIZE (header_cfg.h.jinja2), which is NOT gated (DD62/F6: it is additive and
    inert with the gate off, not byte-identical, and is not protected by this same property test,
    which reads source_cfg only). #}
    {{'0x%02Xu' % ((configuration.programming.max_block_size | default(8))
                   if (configuration.programming.enabled | default(false)) else 0)}}, /* maxBsPgm */
