    preserving here rather than deleting, because it is the second time this template has made it.
    The dispatcher not READING a byte does not make the byte identical: design doc Section 9's
    criterion is byte-for-byte identity of the GENERATED FILE with the gate off, and six settings
    changed it (measured, one per bit, at the generated `(0x00u << 0x0Nu)` lines). Inert on the wire
    is not the test.

    The paragraph then cited the two configuration tests as confirmation, which was the real error:
    it read "these tests pass" as "the property holds", and said so in as many words ("since neither
    test's own configurations ever set any of these six flags away from their own shared False
